  "worked_solution": "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/47eccc29cbbdd917a247dec2f10329f718ed133b7e8398312b4ee3bc6bbbd647.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\u222c}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{\u222c}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
